- op: discuss  # 47b3
  at: '2026-08-22T01:28:11Z'  # 47b3
  by: agent  # 47b3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 47b3
  clock: 7  # 47b3
  nonce: 47b3  # 47b3
  message: "FIXED AND MERGED (PR #473, dev a34daf706f). STATUS -> pending_validation, NOT\nsatisfied, and the reason is a measurement rather than caution -- see the last\nsection.\n\nTHE FIX, and it is this item's own option (b). `ir._dedupe_key` no longer\ndiscards the path for a `kind=\"file\"` dangler. Each tier-dropped file now gets\n`{lang}:{path}:0-0:file:external_symbol` instead of every such file in a\nlanguage sharing `{lang}:<external>:0-0:file:external_symbol`. The function's own\ndocstring stated the licensing assumption -- the path slot is \"a per-reference\nfilesystem path with no semantic identity\" -- and that sentence was the defect:\nit names the file that did the importing, which is the only thing a reader can\nopen.\n\nMINIMAL REPRO, three lines of PYTHON (this item said javascript):\n\n    \"\"\"@generated\"\"\"\n\n    from datetime import date\n\nCHAIN: is_likely_minified heuristic 3 matches (Generated by|@generated|DO NOT\nEDIT) in the first five lines with NO comment anchor, so a docstring trips it ->\ntier 4 (DERIVED) -> cli.py's tier filter drops the Symbol while DELIBERATELY\nKEEPING its edges (WI-pozur / ADR-0043 C2) -> _dedupe_key discards the path.\n\n*** THIS ITEM'S TWO CLOSURE ROUTES WERE BOTH WRONG DOORS, AND ITS OWN OPTION (b)\nWAS RIGHT. *** Route (a) -- \"demonstrate a LINKER minting a dangling file-id edge\nsrc\" -- is the wrong producer: the offending edges carry origin=[\"python\"], the\nANALYZER, and all three file-id-minting linkers (websocket, vue_component,\njs_module) already synthesize or reuse a Symbol for every path they anchor on. I\nread all three before concluding.\n\nI ALSO SHIPPED THE WRONG FIX FIRST, AND AN EXISTING TEST IS WHAT SAID SO.\nNarrowing cli.py's `_is_valid_edge_src` carve-out to a membership test DROPS the\nedge with the node. It measures BETTER than the right fix (177 edges removed, 0\nadded, 0 first-party nodes lost) and it deletes a dependency fact WI-pozur\ndeliberately preserved: test_phase_de_reorder.py::TestDanglingSourceClosed::\ntest_pb2_import_srcs_resolved requires a tier-dropped *_pb2.py file's protobuf\nimports to survive with resolvable srcs, and failed loudly. Recorded because the\nwrong fix looked better on its metrics.\n\nWI-fozoh's COLLAPSE REVERSED ON A RE-PRICE, NOT AN ARGUMENT. Its test cited \"732\nof these on hypergumbo self-analysis\" -- measured before WI-ramuv's file-Symbol\nsynthesizer existed. Re-measured on that same evidence base today: 1,577 real\nfile Symbols and exactly 3 file-kind boundary anchors. 732 -> 3. The collapse\nbuys no node-count relief any more; it only destroys attribution. Its test is\ninverted and carries the number.\n\nA/B, 5 REPOS, arms differing only in ir.py, per-arm XDG_CACHE_HOME, arm A\nasserted to have the collapse really back before measuring:\n\n    repo         <external> A -> B   relationships lost   new anchors\n    sqlalchemy        149 -> 0              0             3 named files\n    poetry              5 -> 0              0             1\n    knex (JS)          12 -> 0              0             2\n    sops (Go)          11 -> 0              0             2\n    httpx               0 -> 0              0             -  (control, unchanged)\n\nZERO relationships lost -- every (dst,type) previously on the placeholder is\nstill present, now from a real path -- and the anchored-edge count RISES 177 ->\n243 because per-file attribution is RECOVERED. Node cost +2/+1/+1/0/0. THREE\nLANGUAGES, against this item's \"All 19 observed rows are javascript\" and its\n\"NOT DIAGNOSED\" on other languages.\n\nA MEASUREMENT TRAP WORTH RECORDING: a RENAMING fix reads as destructive under a\nnaive (src,dst,type) diff -- my first adjudication reported \"177 edges LOST\",\nwhich was 177 edges whose src changed. Adjudicate on (dst,type) preservation.\n\n*** WHY pending_validation AND NOT satisfied. *** This item is stated about\nFLOWS (\"a reported taint flow must name a source location a reader can open\"), so\nthe natural closure evidence is flow-level. I ran it on sqlalchemy in BOTH arms\nand the two are IDENTICAL: 11 evidence rows, the same four source anchors, the\nsame verdicts, 0 pathless anchors in EITHER arm. The collapsed node never seeded\na flow on that repo, so \"0 pathless source anchors after the fix\" is a property\nof the corpus and not of the change -- the zero-against-zero shape. What\ndiscriminates is the graph-level census above, with httpx as an unchanged\ncontrol. After the fix no <external> node exists for a flow to anchor on, but\nthat is an ENTAILMENT, and the closure-evidence discipline says an entailment may\nsupplement behavioural evidence and never substitute for it.\n\nWHAT WOULD UPGRADE IT TO satisfied: a repo whose taint flows actually traverse a\ngenerated file, so the flow-level before/after is discriminating. This item's own\nfiled population cannot supply it -- mitmproxy's UI is .tsx, which has no taint\ncatalogue.\n\nSPUN OUT: INV-bokim (P1). 2 of hypergumbo's OWN 3 file-boundary anchors are\nhand-written test files whose docstrings mention that some OTHER file is\ngenerated; both contribute 0 nodes to a default survey where a comparable\ntest_ir.py contributes 186. That is a misclassification, not an anchor problem,\nso it is filed rather than folded in here."  # 47b3
