- op: discuss  # e026
  at: '2026-08-22T05:01:40Z'  # e026
  by: agent  # e026
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e026
  clock: 9  # e026
  nonce: e026  # e026
  message: "pending_validation -> SATISFIED on the flow-level evidence this item named as its own\nupgrade condition: \"a repo whose taint flows actually traverse a generated file,\nso the flow-level before/after is discriminating.\"\n\nTHE REPO IS dash.js. Found by SCREENING rather than guessing: 11 repos were run\nin the PRE-FIX arm first (caddy, sops, poetry, mitmproxy, knex, express,\napollo-server, pretix, microservices-demo, containerd, kserve, keda, grafana)\nand every one produced ZERO placeholder-anchored taint rows -- so pairing any of\nthem would have been the zero-against-zero shape this item was downgraded for.\ndash.js produced 6.\n\nSINGLE-HUNK ATTRIBUTION, three arms, so the karud collapse merged in the same\nwindow cannot be mistaken for this fix:\n\n    arm                                          rows   placeholder-anchored\n    A   pre-rozob            26276a8430             4          2\n    B0  post-rozob, pre-karud a34daf706f            2          0\n    B   post-both            200e151682             1          0\n\nThe rozob hunk ALONE takes 4 -> 2 and 2 -> 0. The further 2 -> 1 is INV-karud\ncollapsing the two surviving readable rows into one situation, which is a\ndifferent change and is shown separately rather than folded in.\n\nGRAPH-LEVEL, SAME TWO ARMS:\n    file-boundary anchors      1  ->  7   (each naming its file)\n    edges out of them         32  -> 40   (per-file attribution RECOVERED)\n\n*** AND THE MECHANISM IS READ OFF THE GRAPH RATHER THAN INFERRED. *** The two\nrows do not get RENAMED, they DISAPPEAR, and the reason is visible in the edge\nlist. Pre-fix, one node carried both:\n   sources: document.addEventListener / document.createElement / window.css,\n            all from test/functional/lib/ima3_dai.js (574KB minified IMA SDK)\n   sink:    console.error, from webOSTVjs-1.2.10/webOSTV.js (a webpack bundle,\n            0 newlines)\nThose are DIFFERENT FILES with no call relationship between them. The collapse\nmerged them into one node and the taint walk then read a source and a sink on\none seed as a flow. That is measurement 0001's `unrelated-files` false-positive\nmechanism -- \"source and sink are in two files with no call relationship at\nall\" -- MANUFACTURED BY THE COLLAPSE ITSELF. So the fix does not merely make\nthe rows readable; it removes two rows that were never real.\n\nPOSITIVE CONTROL (L13), run before any of the above was believed. Same two arms\non poetry's GRAPH: arm A holds exactly one\n`python:<external>:0-0:file:external_symbol`; arm B holds zero, and instead\nnames `tests/repositories/fixtures/distribution_hashes.py`. So the mechanism is\nlive and the arms took. Note the drift the earlier A/B recorded as poetry 5 -> 0\nnow measures 1 -> 0, which is why the control was re-run rather than quoted.\n\nWHAT THE SEARCH ALSO ESTABLISHED, and it is worth keeping. The population is\nRARE, and structurally so: a tier-dropped file is disproportionately vendored,\nminified or test code, and taint sources rarely sit in it. Two of dash.js's own\nseven named anchors are hand-written test files\n(test/unit/test/streaming/streaming.net.FetchLoader.js is 22 lines of chai),\nwhich is INV-bokim's misclassification class showing up in this evidence rather\nthan a separate finding.\n\nMEASUREMENT NOTE: the screen ran with --include-non-production-sources\ndeliberately. Tier-dropped files are mostly under test/ and samples/, and the\ndefault production scope (WI-bifob) would have hidden exactly the population\nbeing looked for. dash.js's verdicts are unchanged by the flag in both arms\n(excluded_flows is empty in both), so it did not manufacture the result."  # e026
